<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pretoria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pretoria is the administrative capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauteng">Gauteng</a> province. Founded in 1855 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthinus-wessel-pretorius">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius</a> and named after his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-pretorius">Andries Pretorius</a>, it became the capital of the South African Republic in 1860 and later of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> Colony. Since the Union of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 1910 it has been the seat of the national government, and its Union Buildings house the presidency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pretoria.jpg" alt="Pretoria" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davinci77 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uniegebou.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
